From 9915012299c1419ad6a3ed7585e932326bdc0af7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: William Porter <liam@wporter.org>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 00:06:11 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] fix(delegate): make output_schema a strict raw-JSON contract

- Parent prompt: static structured-output guidance, only when delegate_task
  is loaded (cache-safe).
- Child prompt: OUTPUT CONTRACT is the final system-prompt block; the
  prose-summary instructions are omitted when a schema is set (leaf and
  orchestrator). Schema-less prompts are byte-identical to before.
- Validation parses the whole response; fenced or prose-wrapped JSON is a
  contract miss (one bounded retry remains).
- Summary budget never truncates a schema-valid result, so the parent
  always receives parseable JSON.
